<title>ZIMBABWE: African Distillers half-year shr rises.</title>
<headline>African Distillers half-year shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-yr ended September 30.</p>
<p>	     (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)				     11.1 vs 8.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)					3.7 vs 2.7</p>
<p>    Operating income			    16.9 vs 15.7</p>
<p>    Interest payable			     0.6 vs 3.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax income				16.3 vs 12.6</p>
<p>    Taxation					 7.3 vs 5.7</p>
<p>    Attrib. income				 9.0 vs 6.9</p>
<p>    Turnover				     115.1 vs 103.5</p>
<p>Div payable December 6 on register November 22.</p>
<p>Full name: African Distillers Limited</p>
<p>NOTE:- The company said it expected a boost in demand for its products as early indications were that the country was due to have normal rains this season. It said a similar trend in profitability could be expected in the second half of the financial year.</p>
<p>----Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
